From fe2320ba7cd47c8216817c265418227bf94069b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pablo Lopez <plopez@unc.edu.ar>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:11:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Print an estimate of the memory (RAM) needed by the run

Before reading the particle data (as soon as the number of particles is
known) DTFE prints the estimated peak memory in GB, highlighted. The
estimate is an empirical model (src/io/memory_estimate.h) calibrated with
29 measured runs (2.6e5-2.1e6 particles, grids 64^3-192^3, 1-27 threads,
1-512 partitions; within -15%/+18%). It accounts for the particle data
size (compiled fields), the Delaunay triangulations computed at the same
time (partitions, threads and padding), the grid fields requested and the
data reading peak. Also added to the Makefile dependencies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C44ZCErHKsQgk681XW3FMn
